th the cash for  almost everyone the budget iPad gets the  a10 processor compared to the 812 on the  2019 iPads in the a 12 X on the pro the  budget iPads a10 is also the only one  that doesn't come with the knurl engine  getting into the Geekbench 4 benchmark  the budget iPad is way behind the others  in terms of single core and even more  behind in multi-core with the air and  mini  almost doubling the score in the pro  almost tripling the score in the metal  test the air and mini are around 75%  faster than the budget iPad and the iPad  pro is almost 2 times faster than the  2019 iPads in over 3 times faster than  the budget iPad in antutu 3d benchmark  there isn't as big of a difference now  but the iPad pro is still around two and  a half times faster than the 2018 budget  iPad finally for a more realistic test  we exported a one-minute 4k 60p video on  each of the iPads and the iPad pro  finished four times sooner than the  budget iPad it was over twice as fast as  a 2019 iPads this is where you'll  actually feel a difference on the new  iPad pro and now let's talk about gaming  each of these iPads apart from the  budget iPad can run fortnight at high  graphics at 60 frames per second the  budget iPad  only run medium graphics at 30 frames  per second and that's the same story for  other games like asphalt 9 running at 30  instead of 60 like on the more expensive  iPads the graphics are noticeably worse  and I also noticed some dropped frames  while gaming the iPad air mini and pro  all run fortnight and asphalt 9  perfectly at 60 frames per second no  dropped frames are issues at all so the  extra power of the pro isn't really  being used in almost every game on the  App Store out of all of them the iPad  Mini is by far the most comfortable to  hold in the hand while gaming the others  weigh quite a bit more so your hands  will get tired over time let's quickly  mention some other spec differences  before I start recommending which iPad  you should buy the budget iPad gets  Bluetooth 4.2 compared to 5.0 on the  other iPads which also gets simultaneous  dual band Wi-Fi for more bandwidth and a  more reliable connection they also get  gigabit class LTE if you're buying that  model now with all that said which iPad  should you buy well the iPad pro is  obviously the best and most powerful  iPad but is also the most expensive at  $800 the four speakers and pro motion  technology make a huge difference in  daily use but if you're not going to be  doing high-end editing or anything that  can actually use the power of the a 12 X  chip you'll probably be better off  buying the 2019 iPad air if you've got  the extra cash you love the design and  you want to keep it for over five years  the iPad pro may be worth the investment  since software will soon catch up to the  amazing hardware also if you're a  serious artist the laminated display  promotion tech and Apple pencil to make  it the best option for drawing and you  can get the pro in the 12 point 9 inch  size as well now the iPad air is the  best all-around iPad since it gets all  the amazing display tech the 10.5 in  size is great for most people and the  a12 processor is really powerful it can  run most apps and games of the 8 12 X  can it'll also be fast enough for most  photo editing tasks as well the new air  is also the only non Pro iPad that comes  with a smart connector so if you're  planning on getting the smart keyboard  and you don't want to spend the extra  cash on the pro the air is a great  all-around long-term option for the  price now the Mini is literally  identical to the air and almost  everything except that it doesn't get  the smart connector in it  it's the same amount of pixels in a  smaller display so it looks sharper if  you get up close to it it's also $100  cheaper than the air so you can save a  good amount of cash if you're fine with  the small display I'd also like to say  that if you play a lot of games the mini  is the best choice since it's so  comfortable to hold for longer gaming  sessions it's small light and portable  so it'll be a great option for the kids  as well now the budget iPad will also be  a good option for kids  since the non laminated display is  really cheap to replace it's the slowest  out of the bunch the display and cameras  are worse but it's also the cheapest  especially if you can find it for only  $250 on Amazon click the link below to  see if it's still on sale it's a great  budget option for everyone who just  needs a basic iPad to do iPad things and  it'll be fine for most of the popular  games on the App Store well there you  have it if this comparison didn't help  you make a decision comment below with  your specific situation and we'll help  you out if you enjoy this video click  that subscribe button above for more  videos like this one this has been  defeating with Max sec thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

